secubox-rustdesk (1.0.8-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Apply dual-vhost MUST pattern (docs/MODULE-GUIDELINES.md §4):
    /rustdesk/ on the canonical hub vhost is now `alias /usr/share/
    secubox/www/rustdesk/` (static admin page), no longer a proxy to
    the RustDesk web admin LXC. NEW dedicated vhost
    `/etc/nginx/sites-available/rustdesk.conf` for
    `rustdesk.gk2.secubox.in` (Authelia-gated) serves the real web
    admin at the root path.
  * The signal/relay TCP/UDP ports (21115-21119) are unaffected —
    they go through HAProxy stream-mode + nftables DNAT, not nginx.
  * Operator-side prerequisites for the new vhost: DNS + TLS cert +
    HAProxy ACL + mitmproxy route (documented in
    nginx/rustdesk-vhost.conf header).
  * rustdeskctl emit_access_json: real web-admin URLs — lan
    `http://10.100.0.90:21114/` + public
    `https://rustdesk.gk2.secubox.in/`. Scope renamed `lan-web` -> `lan`
    and `public-web` -> `public` to match sibling modules (the
    rustdesk:// scopes lan-signal/lan-relay stay as-is).
    Default PUBLIC_HOSTNAME -> rustdesk.gk2.secubox.in.
  * rustdeskctl config_get strips TOML inline comments.
  * www/rustdesk/index.html: "native UI" button reads from /access,
    skipping the rustdesk:// scopes (they're for the desktop client).

 -- Gerald Kerma <devel@cybermind.fr>  Sun, 24 May 2026 10:32:00 +0200

